---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TrustBar from '../components/TrustBar.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About Us | Coastal Property Restorations | Punta Gorda, FL"
  description="Meet the team behind Coastal Property Restorations — licensed, bonded, insured, and based in Punta Gorda, serving Southwest Florida homeowners."
  breadcrumb="About Us"
>
  <TrustBar />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 46rem;">
      <h1>About Coastal Property Restorations</h1>

      {/* TODO: owner headshot + a crew/truck photo belong here — customers hire
          people, not logos (spec §5). Left out rather than shipping a placeholder. */}

      {/*
        TODO: replace with Sean's story in his own words — when and why he started
        the company, what Ian recovery was like, why local answers differently than
        a franchise. The copy below is honest and grounded in real projects, but
        his actual voice will outperform it.
      */}
      <p>
        Coastal Property Restorations is a local, owner-operated company based in
        Punta Gorda. Sean runs the jobs himself — he is the one who shows up for the
        estimate, and he is on site while the work happens.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work across Charlotte and Lee County: Punta Gorda, Port Charlotte, Fort
        Myers, and out onto Pine Island. That means older coastal homes, stilt homes,
        canal-side properties, and buildings that have been through Charley and Ian
        both. Very little of it is standard, and a fair amount of what we open up
        turns out to hide something nobody knew about — a slow leak, dry rot, water
        behind a wall. We would rather find it and fix it right than cover it up.
      </p>
      <p>
        We handle the whole job: roofing and storm damage, water damage from
        emergency response through rebuild, and the remodel side — kitchens,
        bathrooms, flooring, drywall, and paint. One company, one point of contact,
        from the insurance claim to the final coat of paint.
      </p>

      <h2>Licensed, Bonded &amp; Insured</h2>
      <p>
        Most Florida contractors carry a license and insurance. We also carry a
        bond — an extra layer of financial protection most companies skip. If
        something ever went wrong, you're covered. That's peace of mind you can
        verify, not just a slogan.
      </p>
      {/* TODO: add license number(s), bond and insurance details, and any
          manufacturer certifications as a list here once Sean provides them. */}

      <h2>Where We Work</h2>
      <p>
        Based at {site.address.street}, {site.address.city}, {site.address.state} —
        serving Punta Gorda, Port Charlotte, Fort Myers, and surrounding Southwest
        Florida communities. <a href="/service-areas">See all service areas →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand heading="Talk to us — no pressure, no obligation." emergency={false} />
</Base>
